{"t": 1794106455.939265, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Heads up: this PR introduced a production reconciliation bug.\n\nSentry issue: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/ (ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit, expected 1100, got 1099; first seen in release 2026.11.3, 2,201 events).\n\nThe change to `worker/rates.py` replaced decimal rounding with `int(amount_minor * rate)`, which truncates. When the product lands just below a whole minor unit (e.g. 1099.999... from float error), the result is one minor unit short.\n\nFix: `worker/rates.py` now uses `Decimal(amount_minor) * Decimal(str(rate))` and quantizes with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, restoring rounding to the nearest minor unit.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794106457.6466532, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_pull_request_read", "args": {"method": "get_comments", "owner": "acme", "perPage": 20, "pullNumber": 412, "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
