{"t": 1794106481.9024725, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Update on the fix: to keep the pre-change rounding semantics, `worker/rates.py` restores `round(amount_minor * rate)` instead of the `int(...)` truncation introduced here. That is the minimal revert and clears the LEDGER-WORKER-9A mismatch (1100 vs 1099).\n\nError link: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
